%% Resilience scenario 3 (inclusive hierarchical): when the secondary
%% fast memory pool fails, the slow host DRAM pool is a SUPERSET, so
%% every block that was in fast also exists in slow. Recovery is a
%% prefetch from slow → HBM. No re-prefill needed.
flowchart LR
    Acc["Accelerator"]
    HBM["HBM"]
    Acc --- HBM

    SecMem["Secondary fast memory pool<br/>(unresponsive)"]:::dead
    Slow["Slow host DRAM pool<br/>(superset of fast<br/>— still has every block)"]:::ok

    HBM x--x|fast tier offline| SecMem
    HBM ==>|"prefetch missing<br/>blocks from slow"| Slow
    Slow ==>|"warm KV back into<br/>HBM, requests resume"| HBM

    classDef dead fill:#fee,stroke:#c00,stroke-dasharray:5 5
    classDef ok fill:#e6f0ff,stroke:#1a4d99
